These recipes fetch vendor inputs from official sources and process them locally.
The repository contains preparation code, not the vendor binaries. Source-code
licensing and redistribution of generated vendor assets are separate matters.

Project files with an explicit SPDX license retain that license. The Rust SGX
implementation and its assembly declare GPL-2.0-only. The isgx ABI attribution
and accompanying Intel License.txt are preserved. Other project Rust sources do
not yet have a blanket license; LicenseRef-Unspecified records that gap, not a
new license grant. Resolve it before distributing a project runtime package.
The locked Rust dependencies retain their own licenses; their license texts are
installed under goodix-milanl-engine/dependencies in the package license directory.

The separately built goodix-milanl-oem package contains original Goodix/Huawei
and Intel vendor content, including reconstructed enclave pages. Reconstruction
does not change the vendor license. Keep this package local and private; do not
upload it, extracted binaries, or a vendor-containing source bundle to a public
repository or package service. The extracted gfspi.inf copyright notice and
Intel Software License Agreement accompany that local package. Preserve the
original installers and consult their terms; these recipes confer no additional
rights and do not silently accept an installer license on the user's behalf.

No fingerprint templates, PMK, OTP data, image pixels or host secrets belong in
any of these packages.
